WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
- [Marc Vines-Bright:] Adonis is destined for greatness.

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:09.884
He has something that most sighted people don’t have, and that’s vision.

00:00:11.094 --> 00:00:12.595
He has a vision of his future.

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:17.017
He has a vision of what he wants in this world, and he’s not afraid to get it.

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:24.649
- [Adonis Watt:] Having sight or not having sight doesn’t really matter to me.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:26.651
There’s no room for fear.

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:36.745
So technically I guess you could say I’m completely blind.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:45.295
My mind, it’s almost like a TV that’s runnin’ 24/7. Images flash.

00:00:46.296 --> 00:00:47.881
- Adonis, here I am.

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:53.470
- [Adonis:] It’s basically like I see ‘em, even though I really can’t.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.972
It’s like an illusion in a way.

00:01:01.811 --> 00:01:04.939
- [Veronica:] As an early child, Adonis was so jovial.

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:08.568
He was laughter all the time. We signed him up for football.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.945
We bought his cleats that morning; we went swimming.

00:01:10.945 --> 00:01:16.326
That was the day he lost his eyesight, so he never actually wore the cleats on the field.

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:22.165
- [Adonis:] Went underwater. I came up, and I couldn’t really see.

00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:30.090
- [Veronica:] He has a very rare congenital glaucoma. One in 10,000 kids have this.

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:34.385
And it just so happened that I was there alone with him in the pool.

00:01:34.385 --> 00:01:36.137
It could have happened at any time.

00:01:36.137 --> 00:01:44.938
The next, like, I wanna say three or four years, I had 12, 12 eye surgeries. I hated them.

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:51.069
I would wake up, and it was like I didn’t have control of nothin’.

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:55.240
I would just woke up, like, just cryin’ for no reason.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:02:00.537
You take for granted, like, the street or the grass or the sky, you know?

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:02.455
Just regular stuff like that outside.

00:02:04.415 --> 00:02:06.292
- He says, “Mom, I gotta get ready to get back on the field.”

00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:11.673
I wanted to say, “They’re not gonna accept you. They’re not gonna let you play.

00:02:14.008 --> 00:02:16.177
And I said to him, “You’re gonna get hit on your blind side.”

00:02:16.177 --> 00:02:19.013
And he says, “Mom, all my sides are blind. I know that.”

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.311
- [Adonis:] The only challenge I could, like, really remember

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.772
was gettin’ my parents to listen to me more.

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:32.819
They would hold me back.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:37.031
Kinda had to find a way to convince ‘em to just let me go.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:45.373
Other people probably do put limits on me. It’s just because they don’t know no better.

00:02:47.584 --> 00:02:48.960
- [Sanaa Watt:] No, 2-1.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.962
- First one doesn’t count.

00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:52.463
- No, I made two.

00:02:52.463 --> 00:02:54.174
- Thinkin’ about blind people, you think of, like,

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:56.384
Stevie Wonder and, like, Ray Charles and all them.

00:02:56.384 --> 00:02:59.888
I’m playin’ football and doin’ basketball and runnin’ track

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:02.015
and doin’, all this, like, athletic stuff.

00:03:02.765 --> 00:03:05.310
One more and I win.

00:03:14.485 --> 00:03:18.198
To play basketball, I line up my phone with the net and then scoot it back

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:22.327
so it’s, like, under the backboard. Then I’ll play music.

00:03:22.327 --> 00:03:25.079
♪♪♪

00:03:25.079 --> 00:03:28.374
- Your net’s here. Nope. Jump.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:32.295
- Hold this real quick.

00:03:32.295 --> 00:03:35.465
And I’ll use the music to aim where I’m shooting at

00:03:40.929 --> 00:03:46.226
If there was a miracle to happen, I’d probably end up playin’ basketball

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:50.104
cuz, let’s just be honest, I got the body of a basketball player,

00:03:50.104 --> 00:03:53.691
and before I went blind, I was always hoopin’.

00:03:56.653 --> 00:03:59.405
- [Veronica:] I tried to trick him. I’ve tried to delay him.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:05.036
I tried to put him in different sports. He will not be blocked.

00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:12.126
- Even in flag football, I was playin’, I was playin’ center.

00:04:12.126 --> 00:04:19.550
So, I mean, I ain’t really get to, like, get the ball until probably I was, like, nine or 10.

00:04:22.512 --> 00:04:25.765
- [Veronica:] It’s when he lost his eyesight he gained a whole new vision for his life.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:31.354
He sees himself as, like, the strongest, the biggest, the fastest, the smartest, the most agile.

00:04:31.354 --> 00:04:34.649
Like, he really believes he’s unstoppable.

00:04:34.649 --> 00:04:41.197
- [Marc:] There we go. Big breath in, and exhale as you come back up.

00:04:42.407 --> 00:04:45.368
Right side, there we go. And down.

00:04:45.368 --> 00:04:48.496
- [Adonis:] To me, football has always been football, always gonna be football.

00:04:48.496 --> 00:04:51.207
I wanna get faster, get stronger. I wanna get bigger.

00:04:51.207 --> 00:04:53.751
There wasn’t even a thought of quitting.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:05:00.466
- We’re workin’ on, really, strength, stability, uh, balance, or proprioception.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:05.596
Later on down the line, it’s going to have to be building mass because he's gonna

00:05:05.596 --> 00:05:09.100
take some hits because he’s not gonna be able to see everything comin’ at him.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.564
- [Adonis:] Usin’ a cane’s kinda like an ongoing thing. You’re never, like, perfect at it,

00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:18.401
but I guess you could say it took me four, maybe five years.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:23.489
With Braille in general, learning how to read and write

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:27.076
probably took me, like, three years to be pretty good at it

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:35.209
Right here says, “I’m going to the NFL.”

00:05:37.211 --> 00:05:42.633
As far as usin’ my phone, I was cool after, like, two weeks.

00:05:42.633 --> 00:05:48.973
So I do this, slide it up. So nobody can hear what I’m textin’,

00:05:48.973 --> 00:05:51.642
who I’m textin’, I speed up the speech.

00:05:52.393 --> 00:05:55.855
Whatever I tap,  it says what I tap.

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:59.734
I basically remembered every letter in the keyboard,

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:03.696
so I just text like anybody else, and it sends ‘em out a text basically.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:08.034
[Accelerated phone speech]

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:11.371
A lot, a lot of this stuff, as far as knowin’ where things is,

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:15.375
is just guessing games. And I don’t know if it’s, like, a feeling, but it's like

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:19.879
something goes off in my brain, like an alarm sayin’ I’ve been here before.

00:06:21.255 --> 00:06:23.841
- [Scott Heideman:] When you hear as a football coach that you’re gonna

00:06:23.841 --> 00:06:27.553
have a blind athlete come in and wanna play football, it was challenging.

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:33.309
The thought of, of somebody playing a position like running back

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:35.186
and not being able to see, it’s hard to wrap your mind around.

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:40.608
- [Adonis:] To be honest, I don’t think they completely,

00:06:40.608 --> 00:06:43.069
completely believed that I could play running back.

00:06:46.114 --> 00:06:47.740
- He doesn’t want anything given to him.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.785
And when, you know, when we told the officials in his first game

00:06:50.785 --> 00:06:53.329
where he scored a touchdown—he scored that touchdown based on the team

00:06:53.329 --> 00:06:57.083
making a very sportsman-like action by letting him score.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:07:00.545
But everybody around him knew that’s not what he wanted.

00:07:00.545 --> 00:07:03.881
When we went into the next game, we didn’t really tell anybody.

00:07:07.552 --> 00:07:09.345
And he scored two touchdowns. It was all earned.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.518
- [Veronica:] Like, he’s not breaking records.

00:07:15.518 --> 00:07:20.273
He’s setting records. Like, he’s the first. The first, the first, the first, the first, the first.

00:07:21.732 --> 00:07:25.278
- [Adonis:] I remember havin’ to actually push through somebody and kinda,

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:27.196
like, almost dive in.

00:07:27.363 --> 00:07:28.948
- [Player:] Get there!

00:07:30.408 --> 00:07:32.118
- [Player:] That’s a touchdown! Let’s go!

00:07:32.118 --> 00:07:35.079
- [Adonis:] It was pretty good knowin’ I could do it

00:07:35.079 --> 00:07:37.123
when somebody was actually tryin’ to stop me.

00:07:41.043 --> 00:07:45.923
- [Marc:] Imagine that in your head there was no other option but to run forward

00:07:45.923 --> 00:07:51.762
and to run into that swarm. That’s where Adonis is. He has no choice.

00:07:54.182 --> 00:07:57.685
- We talk about trust all the time, you know? Used to play quarterback.

00:07:57.685 --> 00:07:59.520
I had to trust. Trust my receivers were gonna be in the right spot.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:02.815
Trust those five guys up front, that they were gonna block their guy.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:07.028
And that was with full vision. To trust those guys without vision,

00:08:07.028 --> 00:08:10.490
knowin’ somebody’s tryin’ to hit you, I mean, it’s, it’s phenomenal.

00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:17.830
- [Adonis:] I mean, my teammates is a big part cuz you can’t be by yourself and win.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.875
You know, you need all 11 guys to do, to do their job.

00:08:20.875 --> 00:08:23.753
To know that they got my back is pretty cool.

00:08:25.963 --> 00:08:28.716
- One of the big things we stress here is trust.

00:08:28.716 --> 00:08:32.011
Him following us around, putting his hand on our shoulder—

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:35.223
—all of us look at that, and we trust each other just a little bit more.

00:08:35.223 --> 00:08:38.976
- In football, you can tend to, like, really get selfish and focus on yourself.

00:08:38.976 --> 00:08:41.062
But when you have someone like Adonis there,

00:08:41.062 --> 00:08:44.190
you recognize the importance of teamwork, and helping a fellow brother out.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.527
I remember one practice, I was just messin’ around,

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:50.404
and I, like, tried—I closed my eyes and I was runnin’ through the plays,

00:08:50.404 --> 00:08:54.325
and it was scary, really scary. So I just admire how fearless he is.

00:08:56.285 --> 00:08:59.372
- He doesn’t let him being blind affect anything that he does.

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:01.040
Like, it’s just inspiring to see.

00:09:01.999 --> 00:09:05.378
- [Scott:] The more I spent time with Adonis, the more his blindness disappeared

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:08.005
and the more I just saw him as Adonis the football player,

00:09:08.005 --> 00:09:10.132
less as Adonis the blind football player.

00:09:10.424 --> 00:09:15.137
- [Adonis:] What I like best is probably how hard you have to work,

00:09:15.137 --> 00:09:17.932
how it’s just not given to you.

00:09:18.933 --> 00:09:23.229
You gotta be somebody that’s gonna be, be able to go the extra mile.

00:09:23.229 --> 00:09:30.111
- [Chanting] B-R-O-N-C-O-S, Broncos!

00:09:30.111 --> 00:09:31.862
- [Jason Jewell:] You can’t go out on a pass,

00:09:31.862 --> 00:09:33.781
and it’s tough to see where a blitzer is comin’ from,

00:09:33.781 --> 00:09:34.949
so we gotta limit what we’re doing.

00:09:34.991 --> 00:09:38.911
But last year he scored several touchdowns in short-yardage situations,

00:09:38.911 --> 00:09:41.831
and I’m hopin’ we can do that again in 2019.

00:09:41.831 --> 00:09:45.334
- [Cheering]

00:09:45.334 --> 00:09:49.797
- [Adonis:] After high school, I’mma hopefully go to a D-I school on a scholarship.

00:09:49.797 --> 00:09:54.176
After I produce there, hopefully I can get to the NFL

00:09:54.176 --> 00:09:57.471
and get some rings and play for a long time.

00:09:58.848 --> 00:10:01.809
- [Jason:] I’ve had thoughts of bein’ in a game-winning situation

00:10:01.809 --> 00:10:05.688
on the 1-yard line. How awesome would it be to have Adonis in to score that touchdown?

00:10:07.732 --> 00:10:13.404
- [Veronica:] And his faith actually has been the light that guides me through his darkness.

00:10:14.864 --> 00:10:18.743
- [Announcer:] That’s the end of the game. Final score: Broncos 14, Bears 10.

00:10:18.743 --> 00:10:22.913
Congratulations to head coach Tom Kohrs and the Brophy Broncos.

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:26.417
- [Coach:] But for next week, so—

00:10:26.417 --> 00:10:27.752
- [Veronica:] We’ll be back Tuesday.

00:10:27.752 --> 00:10:29.462
- Hope you can stay out with varsity.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:31.380
Yeah, Tuesday morning is when—we’re not practicing Monday.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:32.715
- [Veronica:] Perfect, yeah.

00:10:32.715 --> 00:10:33.674
- All right.

00:10:33.674 --> 00:10:35.176
- All right. Thanks, Coach.

00:10:35.176 --> 00:10:35.801
- All right.

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:36.802
- [Veronica:] All right. Thanks, Coach.

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:37.803
- Good season, Adonis.

00:10:37.803 --> 00:10:38.804
- Thank you, Coach.

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:46.062
- [Adonis:] I mean, I think I would’ve ended up the way I am right now anyway, blind or not.

00:10:46.062 --> 00:10:51.233
I mean, I guess you could say it gave, it gave me a little extra layer,

00:10:51.233 --> 00:10:54.236
but, I mean, it didn’t, like, make too much of a difference

00:10:54.236 --> 00:10:56.489
to who I was gonna end up bein’ anyway.

00:10:59.784 --> 00:11:02.536
- [Newscaster:] This is Brophy’s No. 21, Adonis Watt.

00:11:02.536 --> 00:11:06.207
We brought you this story last year—a blind freshman running back on the freshman team,

00:11:06.207 --> 00:11:10.753
and tonight, making his varsity debut, scores from a yard out!

00:11:10.753 --> 00:11:12.505
Yeah, that’s special. That’s big-time!

00:11:12.505 --> 00:11:16.384
Congrats to Adonis Watt. Brophy stays unbeaten—

00:11:30.147 --> 00:11:33.693
♪♪♪

00:11:34.402 --> 00:11:38.197
- [Yelling and cheering]

00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:39.990
- [Larry Fitzgerald:] How you guys doin’ today?

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:40.991
- [Yelling] Good!

00:11:40.991 --> 00:11:43.035
- Good, good. Well, I appreciate you guys lettin’ me come in.

00:11:43.035 --> 00:11:45.329
Anybody know where my man Adonis is?

00:11:45.329 --> 00:11:47.790
- [Yelling] Yeah!

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.583
- Adonis, how you doin’, man?

00:11:49.583 --> 00:11:50.584
- What’s up, bro?

00:11:50.584 --> 00:11:51.419
- Good to see you, brother. You doin’ well?

00:11:51.419 --> 00:11:51.961
- Yes, sir.

00:11:51.961 --> 00:11:54.296
- Man, when I heard about you, man, like: “I gotta go over and meet my guy.

00:11:54.296 --> 00:11:55.923
Man, I gotta, I gotta see this man.”

00:11:55.923 --> 00:11:59.301
You’re much taller than I thought. You almost taller than me.

00:11:59.301 --> 00:12:02.430
- So, you know, it’ll just be the two of us on the team are the only two guys

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:04.849
that have ever played ball with Fitz. Just me and you, Adonis.

00:12:04.849 --> 00:12:06.809
- That’s crazy. You got a ring, though.

00:12:06.809 --> 00:12:10.563
- Well, you’re right. I got—I’m one up on you there. I’m one up on Fitz there too!

00:12:10.563 --> 00:12:11.522
- Yeah!

00:12:11.522 --> 00:12:13.774
- [Larry:] We gonna walk out to the field now, OK? All right.

00:12:13.774 --> 00:12:15.901
- You good if I just hold your shoulder?

00:12:15.901 --> 00:12:17.361
- Yeah, yeah, it’s all good.

00:12:18.279 --> 00:12:22.199
Bein’ blind since he was five years old, he’s never given up his passion for sports,

00:12:22.199 --> 00:12:25.870
and that’s what’s inspiring to me. I’ve played football since I was his age,

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:28.205
and I couldn’t imagine not bein’ able to see.

00:12:28.205 --> 00:12:31.584
But Adonis has beaten all the odds. Teammates are helpin’ him

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:34.378
be able to live his dream as well, and that’s what I love about sports.

00:12:34.378 --> 00:12:36.839
- So this your 16 or 17?

00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:38.507
- Sixteen. Yeah.

00:12:38.507 --> 00:12:40.426
- So how, how you play so long?

00:12:40.426 --> 00:12:42.178
- Uh, the Lord, the Lord’s been good to me.

00:12:42.178 --> 00:12:45.347
Adonis, we’re here on the football field where you scored your touchdowns.

00:12:45.347 --> 00:12:47.641
I wanna play a little quarterback, so I wanna reenact it.

00:12:47.641 --> 00:12:48.976
I’m ready when you are.

00:12:48.976 --> 00:12:50.436
- Yeah, let’s go.

00:12:50.436 --> 00:12:53.814
- Let’s do it. All right, Adonis, they’re about to snap it.

00:12:53.814 --> 00:12:55.775
- All right. Hey, line me up so I’m good.

00:12:55.775 --> 00:12:56.984
- Yeah, you’re good. You’re good.

00:12:56.984 --> 00:12:58.360
- All right. All right.

00:13:01.071 --> 00:13:03.616
- Set, go!

00:13:06.952 --> 00:13:08.621
- [Cheering]

00:13:08.621 --> 00:13:10.581
- Let’s go, Don!

00:13:10.581 --> 00:13:11.582
- Don Don!

00:13:12.208 --> 00:13:13.209
- Attaboy!

00:13:13.209 --> 00:13:14.001
- [Adonis:] Yes, sir.

00:13:14.001 --> 00:13:15.377
- [Larry:] Good job, brother. Good job.

00:13:15.377 --> 00:13:16.754
I really appreciate you allowin’ me to come out here

00:13:16.754 --> 00:13:19.131
and, uh, practice a couple plays with you.

00:13:19.131 --> 00:13:21.842
You’re a wonderful young man and a true inspiration

00:13:21.842 --> 00:13:25.012
and thank you for lettin’ me come out here and be a part of your day.

00:13:25.012 --> 00:13:26.180
- All right, man, thank you.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.932
Thank you for comin’ out here and messin’ with me, dawg. I appreciate it.

00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:28.891
- Absolutely, a pleasure. It’s a pleasure.

00:13:28.891 --> 00:13:30.184
- [Offscreen:] One, two, three…

00:13:30.184 --> 00:13:31.811
- [Together:] Bleacher Report!

00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:33.437
- [Offscreen:] The revenge of the Birds, baby.

00:13:34.855 --> 00:13:36.607
- [Laughing]

00:13:37.107 --> 00:13:38.108
- [Offscreen:] Yeah, can we put this on Bleacher Report’s story?

00:13:39.235 --> 00:13:40.236
- Tag me!

00:13:42.029 --> 00:13:45.032
- I’m Larry Fitzgerald, and this is Bleacher Report.

